## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- a9 says “some judgments” and “not a usual result” reverse the English. The English columns still say courts generally impose about three, four, and six months. R3 requires the softened form already in the Tamil (“in some judgments … there is no typical or guaranteed outcome”). That half was not restored. சிறை was added.
- a14 and b13 are right that U+200B is not Tamil punctuation. The same marks are in the Korean source, and the checker requires an equal count. Promoting Q16–Q20 to ## headings would also change heading levels. Not applied.
- b15 is right that 013 and 015 read as chopped notes. The Korean source is chopped the same way. Merging blocks fails the checker. Not applied.
- a21 is right that “1.57M” is an English abbreviation and that Tamil Nadu and Sri Lanka group by lakh. ACCEPTED-ROUND forbids both the reformat of the pinned bio figure and lakh grouping. Not applied.
- a2 is right that the URL is the withholding-rate standard, not Business Tax Act article 10. The name was corrected. “பிரிவு 3” was not written: it fails numbers against Korean 제10조. The leftover digit 10 is a checker constraint.

